        "content": "THE DEMIURGE OF GOD\n\n(Speaking of the Son of God and identifying Him with the pre-existent Wisdom spoken of in Proverbs viii. 22, Lactantius adds :)\n\n1 Sc. the Logos as Cosmos. 2 Gf. Frag. x.\n\n3 For last clause, see (7, H., i. 12. Gf. also Ps. Augustin., 0. Quinque Hcereses, vol. viii., Append, p. 3 E, Maur.\n\n4 Lactantius himself also gives a partial translation of this passage in his Epitome, 42 (Fritz., ii. 140).\n\nWherefore also Trisinegistus has called Him the \"Demiurge of God.\"1"
